## Performance budgets — ceilings, not gates

Resource budgets guide the orchestrator; they never block delivery by themselves.

| Profile | Subagents | Parallel subagents | Reviewers | Context turns |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| DIRECT | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| LIGHT | up to 2 | up to 2 | 1 by default | 8 |
| FULL | up to 4 | up to 4 | up to 3 | 16 |

Use fewer resources whenever the objective is already reachable. A worker that hits its turn budget returns partial findings + unknowns; the parent decides whether the unknowns matter instead of automatically spawning another loop.

Lexical shards stay tiny and do not preload the full Context Delivery skill. The FULL scout may use the configured provider, but its output remains compact.

After a run, `python3 .harness/lib/council_cost_report.py --run-id <id> --profile <profile>` summarizes observed subagent models, tool calls, tokens and duration when the runtime reported them. Missing metrics are `UNAVAILABLE`; the report is observational and must never become a completion gate.
